        [
          "🗣️ 7. Quick Interview Answers"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8012-816a-f6102d1a8ec4",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Q: What are Spring Boot Starters and Auto-Configuration?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80a2-bf8d-f73de13edbda",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "“A Spring Boot Starter is a pre-defined dependency bundle that simplifies setting up specific features—like web or data access—without configuring each library manually. Auto-Configuration is a Spring Boot feature that automatically sets up components like a web server or database connection by inspecting the project’s libraries. Together, they help developers focus on business logic instead of boilerplate setup.”"
        ]
      ]
    },
